Author: Kenneth Jiang <k@obico.io>
Date:   Wed Sep 16 13:11:23 2026 +0000

    Read the helper's paths through the wide Windows APIs

    Windows hands main() its arguments and getenv() its values in the active
    code page, which cannot spell every path. fs::u8path(argv[i]) therefore
    could not open the bridge tests' "discovery 打印.json", every call fell
    back to the offline catalog, and the eight live-peer tests failed on
    Windows only - from well before M0. The helper now takes anything that
    becomes a path from CommandLineToArgvW and GetEnvironmentVariableW.
    POSIX still compiles the original fs::u8path calls.

    The same run caught the offline catalog still asserted at a pre-M0 size.
    Like the shell harness in dc31f9d3d9, it no longer carries a number: the
    roster belongs to the registry's tests, and over the wire what matters is
    that a shaped catalog arrives.

    The guide's verification section now records the cause instead of an
    unexamined platform gap.

